sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg k_sigma at 1.12 µm in the E. rowelli ocellus (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 83.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 calibrates Schnakenberg (a=0.12, b=0.88, Du=1, Dv=22, seed 3223) so the fastest Turing mode is 14 cycles on a 15.68 µm patch (λ = 1.12 µm). Explicit linear PDE versus continuum dispersion: Pearson r = 0.9915, RMSE = 1171 on the growth-rate scale, KS = 0.069. Saturated DCT peak is quantized at 14.25 cycles (λ_2d = 1.100 µm). Equal-diffusion and reversed-ratio controls are both stable, but both report the same k=0 eigenvalue (−4094.7), so the ablation panel does not yet separate them. The GIF is the Alan Couch CC BY 2.0 animal with a 0.16 body-masked gain. Overall 83.3/100 (faithfulness 82.4, reproducibility 85.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 82, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/euperipatoides_rowelli_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 521196 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 289aff418d717fbf67f1043b54685c9835899cedf4230c5acc41bd9c3678bbff (sha256 289aff418d717fbf67f1043b54685c9835899cedf4230c5acc41bd9c3678bbff), spec_fingerprint 345373ab42e0e02cf6b6faa2dc71e527f6cadf8f798b162c003fe87164eb8759. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 345373ab42e0e02cf6b6faa2dc71e527f6cadf8f798b162c003fe87164eb8759; artifact_sha256: 289aff418d717fbf67f1043b54685c9835899cedf4230c5acc41bd9c3678bbff; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/euperipatoides_rowelli_turing_wavelength_s0/euperipatoides_rowelli_specimen.jpg=29166a767a52ae55..., datasets/euperipatoides_rowelli_turing_wavelength_s0/euperipatoides_rowelli_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=953c4f019dafd397..., datasets/euperipatoides_rowelli_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=4bc7e5b005ed9e1a...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics du/dt = a − u + u²v, dv/dt = b − u²v. | E. rowelli ocelli are about 100 µm across, with a lens, a rhabdomeric layer, and screening pigment (Mayer 2006; Kirwan 2018; Ljungholm & Nilsson 2021). | Photoreceptor centres are about 2–3 µm apart; the 2021 optical mesh uses about 2.5 µm. Kirwan 2018 figures microvilli with a 1 µm scale bar.; reconstructed_in_script: γ = 34122.25342711872 is solved so argmax σ(k) = 2π × 14 on the unit domain, i.e. physical wavelength 1.12 µm. | Holocene mode count N = floor(100 µm / 1.12 µm) = 89, against N = 0 for a Cambrian predecessor below a 10 µm preservation floor. | Pearson r = 0.9915 between continuum σ(k) and an eigenvector-seeded explicit linear PDE on modes 3..31.; transfer_boundary: No source measures a Turing wavelength of 1.12 µm in this species. The length is the slot's detail scale, placed in the microvillus/pigment regime those papers describe. | The whole-animal photograph is the CV target. Magnifying the 15.68 µm patch onto the body mask is a visualization, not a claim that skin annuli have period 1.12 µm.; does_not_claim: That 1.12 µm was fitted to a published Turing model of E. rowelli. | That the Couch photograph is an electron micrograph. | That a successor chronospecies exists (the series is 1/1 and extant). | A second independent assessor.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=2.5]: Single builder-assessor. A second provider has not scored this audit.",
            "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=5.0]: Saturated wavenumber is an integer DCT ring (14.25 cycles, λ=1.100 µm) rather than a sub-bin peak against the calibrated 14 cycles / 1.12 µm.",
            "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=3.5]: Equal-diffusion and reversed-ratio controls both return the k=0 eigenvalue −4094.7, so the ablation panel does not show an in-band difference.",
            "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=5.0]: No Sobel orientation-histogram comparison between the specimen crop and the GIF last frame is reported, only a scalar coherency pair.",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Independent second assessor — still builder-scored.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Replace the integer DCT-ring peak with a sub-bin estimate and report λ against 1.12 µm.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Add a Sobel 12-bin orientation-histogram KS (or L1) between the specimen and the GIF last frame.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Report in-band max Re σ for the two controls so they are not identical copies of the k=0 eigenvalue.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.833"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

